]: 18(1358) NOTICE: : <<< OpenAI Reply: 400 Bad Request (Call-ID: SEC11-621160a-721160a-1-fN2W6oO92t5l)\nL94: Jan 16 13:19:57 aigw1 kamailio[1358]: 18(1358) NOTICE: : <<< OpenAI Reply: 400 Bad Request (Call-ID: SEC11-621160a-721160a-1-7iPH8h54T10X)\nL95: Jan 16 13:19:59 aigw1 kamailio[1358]: 18(1358) NOTICE: : <<< OpenAI Reply: 400 Bad Request (Call-ID: SEC11-621160a-721160a-1-x6TIXkeLp519)\nL96: cite6†s-nishihara1 January 16, 2026, 9:39am 2\nL97: \nL98: We’re also using the SIP calling integration to automate phone-based customer support in Japan. Over the past week, we’ve seen an increase in connection failures during specific, short windows (a few minutes at a time), though service typically recovers quickly afterward.\nL99: Could you please investigate whether any recent changes or updates on the OpenAI side might be contributing to these intermittent connection issues?\nL100: \nL101: cite7†Sean-Der January 17, 2026, 3:57am 3\nL102: Hi!\nL103: \nL104: Sorry about this. We had some bugs internally, but they got fixed today! cite8†Realtime API unreliable over SIP - #13 by Sean-Der L105: \nL106:   * The 0 second calls were because the webhook service had OOMed (so we failed right away)\nL107:   * High Latency/Lag was because of internal delay\nL108: \nL109: If you continue to see issues please @ me or send me an email. I am really trying to get this service in a better spot. Thanks for the patience.\nL110:   * cite0†Home L111:   * cite9†Categories L112:   * cite10†Guidelines L113:   * cite11†Terms of Service†openai.com L114:   * cite12†Privacy Policy†openai.com L115: \nL116: Powered by cite13†Discourse†www.discourse.org , best viewed with JavaScript enabled\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGpt-image-1.5 decreased image render quality? - API - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/gpt-image-1-5-decreased-image-render-quality/1371885)\nciteturn30968view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://community.openai.com/t/gpt-image-1-5-decreased-image-render-quality/1371885\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 215\nL0: cite0†OpenAI Developer Community L1: # cite1†Gpt-image-1.5 decreased image render quality? L2: \nL3: cite2†API L4: \nL5: cite3†gpt-image-15 L6: \nL7: cite4†Vivo_Properties January 17, 2026, 5:50pm 1\nL8: I have noticed a significant increase in artifacts in gpt-image-1.5-2025-12-16 when using the endpoint for editing. To investigate this, I re-ran the prompt and rerendered the same images i had rendered in DEC, only to find that the quality has decreased considerably. Specifically, during editing, there are numerous artifacts, the text on packaging is no longer rendered correctly, and the dimensions are distorted.\nL9: \nL10: Has there been a change that has reduced the model’s performance?\nL11: cite4†Vivo_Properties January 17, 2026, 6:32pm 2\nL12: \nL13: GPT REPLIED\nL14: \nL15: Short answer\nL16: \nL17: There has not been an intentional downgrade of image quality, but there have been changes in the editing pipeline and safety constraints that can negatively affect certain high-precision edit use cases, especially ones like yours.\nL18: \nL19: Why December renders look better\nL20: \nL21: Your December images benefited from:\nL22: \nL23:   * Less aggressive edit safety\nL24: \nL25:   * Higher tolerance for text fidelity\nL26: \nL27:   * A closer “copy-then-modify” behavior during edits\nL28: Re-running the same prompt today does not recreate the same internal conditions.\nL29: \nL30: cite5†jeffvpace January 17, 2026, 7:16pm 3\nL31: \nL32: > Has there been a change that has reduced the model’s performance?\nL33: \nL34: I create image edits all the time using gpt-image-1.5 and this is not my experience. Then again, I don’t use text much…\nL35: \nL36: Can you provide an example so that you could be better assisted?\nL37: \nL38: (1) Provide the original image (2) Provide the edited version (3) Provide the prompt\nL39: Also, it would be helpful if you could provide one of your DEC images for comparison.\nL40: \nL41: cite5†jeffvpace January 17, 2026, 7:22pm 4\nL42: \nL43: Can you provide a screen shot of that conversation?\nL44: \nL45: cite4†Vivo_Properties January 18, 2026, 11:53am 5\nL46: \nL47: ORIGINAL - TO EDIT\nL48: \nL49: cite6†IMG_20251230_1324401920×1440 524 KB†us1.discourse-cdn.com L50: \nL51: DEC RENDER - PERFECT! TOP MODEL!!\nL52: \nL53: JANUARY RENDER - EXACTLY SAME PROMPT - THE IMAGE IS GARBAGE - NO COMMERCIAL VALUE AT ALL…\nL54: Remote controls artifact\nL55: Feet of the coffee table, a total mess.\nL56: Original table had four wooden legs → enhanced gets a single black leg in the center.\nL57: \nL58: Pillows on the couch - awful\nL59: \nL60: Zero reliability - Zero commercial value.\nL61: \nL62: We have dozens of other examples comparing renderings from December to those created yesterday 17/JAN. The results are awful and we can provide them upon request.\nL63: We trusted the model and OpenAI, and built an entire application on top of it. However, OpenAI changed the model parameters without any notice, and the results are no longer reliable. It was a mistake to invest time and money into developing this product based on this company. This lack of transparency could damage the company’s reputation and credibility. These are serious matters, and I cannot imagine how they could happen. These are not the tactics of a serious company.\nL64: cite4†Vivo_Properties January 18, 2026, 11:54am 6\nL65: \nL66: DEC RENDER - PERFECT\nL67: \nL68: cite7†dec_render_accurate_perfect_remotecotrols_coffeetable927×615 126 KB†us1.discourse-cdn.com L69: \nL70: cite4†Vivo_Properties January 18, 2026, 11:56am 7\nL71: \nL72: JAN RENDER - GARBAGE\nL73: \nL74: cite8†jan_17_render_innacurate_coffeetable_remotecontrols1121×756 207 KB†us1.discourse-cdn.com L75: \nL76: cite4†Vivo_Properties January 18, 2026, 11:57am 8\nL77: \nL78: GPT SCREENSHOT\nL79: \nL80: cite9†image1392×848 70.7 KB†us1.discourse-cdn.com L81: \nL82: cite10†_j January 18, 2026, 12:02pm 9\nL83: Real answer, not from AI: this topic is in the wrong category.\nL84: \nL85: ChatGPT is a consumer product. OpenAI doesn’t name “gpt-image-1.5” there. You get the “make pictures with ChatGPT” with whatever facility OpenAI wants to deliver.\nL86: \nL87: cite4†Vivo_Properties January 18, 2026, 12:12pm 10\nL88: \nL89: So that means:\nL90: \nL91:   1. Model can be changed under the hood with no transparency?\nL92:   2. API is useless - model is only for consumer use right?\nL93: \nL94: ChatGPT a consumer product? haha\nL95: \nL96: cite10†_j January 18, 2026, 12:33pm 11\nL97: Are you pointlessly asking ChatGPT? That’s what your screenshot shows. Is ChatGPT where you are asking for images also? Or are you truly making API calls, specifying the model, the size, and the output quality parameter?\nL98: The API should be relatively stable, but with the image models, OpenAI has a three-year pattern of modifying the same model name and the quality delivered also.\nL99: You only need to send a request made three years ago to DALL-E 2 and see junk come out of that model today, so there’s definitely not a hands-off policy on the API either.\nL100: \nL101: cite11†VeitB January 18, 2026, 12:37pm 12\nL102: \nL103: Hi,\nL104: \nL105: To help me better understand the issue, are you generating images through ChatGPT or via the API?\nL106: We have not seen similar reports so far, but it would still be useful to understand what might be driving the observed change in performance.\nL107: \nL108: cite4†Vivo_Properties January 18, 2026, 12:50pm 13\nL109: \nL110: cite12†Image†sea2.discourse-cdn.com Vivo_Properties:\nL111: \nL112: > I have noticed a significant increase in artifacts in gpt-image-1.5-2025-12-16 when using the endpoint for editing.\nL113: \nL114: That’s was my initial post.\nL115: What kind of question is that guys? Did you think we use the ChatGPT chat, we have built an ai real estate app for image enhancement.\nL116: \nL117: Of course we use the API. Specifically, we use the endpoint that is dedicated to edits.\nL118: \nL119: /v1/images/edits\nL120: \nL121: cite11†VeitB January 18, 2026, 1:13pm 14\nL122: \nL123: Thanks for confirming. I’ll keep an eye open for more reports.\nL124: I asked because we have seen this time and time again in the forum.\nL125: \nL126: cite10†_j January 18, 2026, 2:33pm 15\nL127: You will notice one peculiar artifact with gpt-image-1.5 on the edits endpoint: the more you iterate, the more the image devolves into a blotchy mess of globs. Like someone painting with a wet sponge dabbed all over the image. There is no more “look at the person change race over 200 trials”, there is \"look at the literal watermarks make a fake texture all over.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFile input parameters to tools - API - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/file-input-parameters-to-tools/1371839)\nciteturn30968view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://community.openai.com/t/file-input-parameters-to-tools/1371839\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 224\n"
